Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person3805"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang tshe spong chos kyi bla ma</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཞང་ཚེ་སྤོང་ཆོས་ཀྱི་བླ་མ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang tshes spong chos kyi bla ma</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshes spong ba chos kyi bla ma</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang tshe spong pa chos kyi bla ma</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa zhang tshes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dmyal ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang tshes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ne'u thog pa chos kyi bla ma</persName><birth notBefore="1041-01-01" notAfter="1090-12-31">after 1041 before 1090</birth><death notBefore="1141-01-01" notAfter="1141-12-31">1141</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4457</idno><idno type="APIS">3805</idno><note type="comment">Third abbot of gSang phu ne'u thog monastery.&#13;
Author of several commentaries, see [R894SIKE]: 405 (zhang tshe spong ba chos kyi bla mas kyang TI ka 'ga' re brtsams).&#13;
Part of the group of the four main disciples of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786) exX0032026-09-0202-25-28 .</note></person><person xml:id="person3831"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phywa pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཕྱྭ་པ་ཆོས་ཀྱི་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa chos seng ge ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' slong chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes chen po phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa chen po cha pa</persName><birth notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</birth><death notBefore="1169-04-23" notAfter="1169-04-23">1169-04-23</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1404</idno><idno type="APIS">3831</idno><note type="comment">The majority of the information available on Phya pa has been provided in [EZ5JXHJY] and [8S7FDMCJ]. Summaries of the same are also found in [LQZU66YX]: 37-40, [F4UK2S8P]: 2-3, and [BW9UR427]: 35-36 (in French).&#13;
&#13;
&#13;
On his birth in 1109, the year of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786)'s passing, see [TM8DW8WA]: 32-33, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5, and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b2-3.&#13;
On the date of his passing in a "sa mo glang" year, see [R894SIKE]: 400, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5 and 6a5. &#13;
[95UZA9Y5]: 40/3/5 (reported in [7FZ3B926]: 111 and [MPRU5QUC]: 206) specifies the day "sa mo glang gi lo'i nag pa zla ba nag po'i phyogs kyi tshes brgyad," i.e., on the 23rd of the third month.&#13;
&#13;
A list of his students is provided in [EZ5JXHJY]: 356, based on [MQB8JGAX]: 297/4, [KL9XTQWI]: I, 454, [4YEPFBIB]: 340-341, [8GL7ZT7Y], fol. 15b3, [VKBZTBWN], fol. 4b7-5a4.&#13;
[FDEWZ2NZ]: 290 also mentions the list of the four "jo sras" from bSod nams dpal's Bla ma rngog pa yab sras rim par byon pa’i rnam thar rin po che’i rgyan gyi phreng ba.&#13;
&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba lists numerous works composed before Phya pa took the see of gSang phu; these include commentaries and summaries on the Five works of Maitreya, the Pramāṇaviniścaya, the Satyadvayavibhaṅga, Madhyamakālaṃkāra, Madhyamakāloka, and  Bodhicaryāvatāra. He mentions having seen these, the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503) and summaries on Madhyamaka, as well as (ID:4505) and (ID:5971). See exX0032026-04-2304-02-58 .&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba does not mention any composition dealing with monastic discipline. &#13;
&#13;
Śākya mchog ldan ([TM8DW8WA], 12-13 and 32) mentions a (doubtful) commentary on the Pramāṇavārttika (ID:3772) in addition to the commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya, and three summaries (small, intermediate, large), the intermediate one being the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503). (Discussed in [EZ5JXHJY]: 357, translated in [8S7FDMCJ]: 59).&#13;
&#13;
Four groups of students are mentioned in Tibetan sources (which do not imply that the members of the respective groups were studying with Phya pa at the same time), with occasional variations:&#13;
&#13;
1) The "Eight Great Lions" (seng chen brgyad). Eight scholars whose names contains the expression "seng ge," likely connoting their expertise in epistemology. The standard list includes gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), Dan 'bag (ID:3840), 'Bru sha (ID:3841), rMa bya (ID:3842), rTsags/rTsegs (ID:4289), Myang/Nyang bran (ID:3844), and gNyal pa/dMyal ma (ID:6679). The eighth one is instead sometimes said to be gTsang pa 'Jam dpal (ID:6336), 'U yug pa (ID:3846), or mTshur ston (DI:4315).&#13;
&#13;
2) The "four sons of noble families" (jo sras mi bzhi) or the "three sons of noble families" (jo sras gsum). They are young noble men of the rNgog (ID:3847), 'Khon (ID:3848), Khu (ID:3849), and gNyos/sMyos (ID:3850). The four are listed in [VKBZTBWN]: 4a7 and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b3, whereas on 16a1 the author speaks of "jo sras gsum." The four are also listed by bSod nams dpal, see [FDEWZ2NZ]: 290.&#13;
&#13;
3) The "three wise ones" (shes rab can mi gsum) or "four wise ones" (shes rab can mi bzhi). The threefold-list in [VKBZTBWN]: 5a1 has rKong po (ID:3852), lHo pa sgom gzan (ID:3853), Par bu ba/sPar phu ba (ID:3854). 'Gar dbang grub (ID:3851) is added in the fourfold list, e.g. in [R894SIKE]: 406.&#13;
&#13;
4) The "three accomplished ones" (grub thob mi gsum). These are students who later became famous masters: Dus gsum mkhyen pa (ID:3855), Phag mo gru pa (ID:3856), gSal sto (ID:3857). The third is sometimes replaced by Zhang tshal (ID:6409), or is suggested to be the latter's direct student.</note></person><person xml:id="person3834"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya dmar ba byang chub grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱ་དམར་བ་བྱང་ཆུབ་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lung rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lungs rgya dmar pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dam pa stod lung pa rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod rgya</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1075-12-31">after 1054 before 1075</birth><death notBefore="1135-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1135 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4749</idno><idno type="APIS">3834</idno><note type="comment">Floruit 1095–1135. [YF8Z2ZGH]: 332 "rGya dmar pa was not only fully learned, but also possessed numerous Tantric secret precepts."</note></person><person xml:id="person3839"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཙང་ནག་པ་བརྩོན་འགྲུས་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags phug pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang nag</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang<