Maybe the same person as the "Chos kyi grags pa" mentioned as lineage successor of gTsang nag pa (ID:3839) and predecessor of gNyal zhig (ID:3887) in Bu ston's lineage of the Pramāṇaviniścaya (ID:3774).</note></person><person xml:id="person3842"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rma bya byang chub brtson 'grus</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྨ་བྱ་བྱང་ཆུབ་བརྩོན་འགྲུས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rma bya rtsod pa'i seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rma bya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">po tjɨj ˑjɨr</persName><birth notBefore="1085-01-01" notAfter="1130-12-31">after 1085 before 1130</birth><death notBefore="1185-01-01" notAfter="1185-12-31">1185</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1982</idno><idno type="APIS">3842</idno><note type="comment">rMa bya's name is rendered in Tangut as Po tjɨj ˑjɨr, in which po tjɨj is a phonetic transcription of "bodhi" [=Tib. byang chub], whereas ˑjɨr means "diligence" [=Tib. brtson 'grus].</note></person><person xml:id="person3887"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཉལ་ཞིག་པོ་འཇམ་པའི་རྡོ་རྗེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dmyal zhig po 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dpal seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam gsar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab blo gros</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mnyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">snyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dmyag zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nyal zhig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa zhig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">yul dbus kyi slob dpon 'jam pa'i rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dnyal pa zhig po</persName><birth notBefore="1130-01-01" notAfter="1200-12-31">after 1130 before 1200</birth><death notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1275-12-31">after 1200 before 1275</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8724</idno><idno type="APIS">3887</idno><note type="comment">Fl. late 12th to early 13th c. [MPRU5QUC] records the name of this abbot as "'Jam dpal seng ge."&#13;
