[AT6DUUJJ]: 23 discusses his dates, suggesting he lived towards the end of the 12th century..&#13;
[5632TFMN]: 313 suggests he may have passed away in ca. 1227.</note></person><person xml:id="person4207"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">me dig pa</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མེ་དིག་པ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sham po me dig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">me tik pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang me dig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal me dig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal mi dig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">me ston</persName><birth notBefore="1050-01-01" notAfter="1099-12-31">after 1050 before 1099</birth><death notBefore="1102-01-01" notAfter="1180-12-31">after 1102 before 1180</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4207</idno></person><person xml:id="person4270"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya grags bsod nams</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱ་གྲགས་བསོད་ནམས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya grags sod</persName><birth notAfter="1140-12-31">before 1140</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4270</idno><note type="comment">Same person as Chu mig rin mo ba rGya grags bsod (ID:3838), the student of Bla ma sPa tshab (ID:3838)?&#13;
It is not certain whether the teacher of rMog cog pa named rGya grags bsod is the same person as the rGya grags bsod quoted for his views on epistemology.</note></person><person xml:id="person4289"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsegs dbang phyug seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྩེགས་དབང་ཕྱུག་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsags dbang phyug seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtsegs ston</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsags dbang seng</persName><birth notBefore="1120-01-01" notAfter="1149-12-31">after 1120 before 1149</birth><death notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1229-12-31">after 1200 before 1229</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4289</idno><note type="comment">Lineage holder in the traditions of Madhyamaka, Perfection of wisdom, Epistemology, and the Treatises of Maitreya ([8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b5-6), abbot of gSang phu (ID:6173) after Phya pa (ID:3831).</note></person><person xml:id="person4294"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khyung po grags se</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཁྱུང་པོ་གྲགས་སེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khyung po grags seng</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khyung po</persName><birth notBefore="0874-01-01" notAfter="1050-12-31">after 874 before 1050</birth><death notBefore="0954-01-01" notAfter="1120-12-31">after 954 before 1120</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4294</idno></person><person xml:id="person5510"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma dkon mchog</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དར་མ་དཀོན་མཆོག</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rin chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi dkon mchog</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma rin chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dharmaratna</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dhar ma rad na</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar dkon</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phu thang dar dkon</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1299-12-31">before 1299</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8408</idno><idno type="APIS">5510</idno><note type="comment">Considered to be identical with gNyal zhig's student Phu thang Dar dkon. See [Q8FCH7LF]: 294, [4LWBNM7B]: 117.</note></person><person xml:id="person5629"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">śāntabhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rab tu zhi ba bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rab du zhi bzang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhi bzang</persName><birth notBefore="0705-01-01" notAfter="0715-12-31">after 705 before 715</birth><death notBefore="0765-01-01" notAfter="0775-12-31">after 765 before 775</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="APIS">5629</idno><note type="comment">Proposed dates: ca. 710-770 (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person5866"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཞང</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5866</idno></person><person xml:id="person6237"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bya yul dkar mo</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བྱ་ཡུལ་དཀར་མོ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">6237</idno></person><person xml:id="person6631"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stag stog pa gnyan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">སྟག་སྟོག་པ་གཉན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stag stog gnyan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa gnyan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyan dar ma seng ge</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1250-12-31">after 1200 before 1250</birth><death notBefore="1313-01-01">after 1313</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">6631</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work5509"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtog ge rigs pa'i rgyan gyi snying po</title><title xml:lang="bo">རྟོག་གེ་རིགས་པའི་རྒྱན་གྱི་སྙིང་པོ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtog ge rigs pa'i brgyan gyi snying po</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bod snga rabs pa'i tshad ma'i spyi don</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1299-12-31">after 1210 before 1299</date><author ref="person:5510">dar ma dkon mchog</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Summary of epistemology with a nested hierarchical structure combined with a threefold chapter division.&#13;
The author follows the system of Phya pa (ID:3831) on key points such as the sevenfold typology of mind, the threefold typology of objects, etc.. &#13;
He frequently refers anonymously to the views of other Tibetan scholars, who are often identified in glosses in instance (ID:5508), notably: rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786), rGya dmar ba (ID:3834), Phya pa (ID:3831), Dan 'bag pa (ID:3840), gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), Me tig pa (ID:4207), etc.</note><idno type="APIS">5509</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5513"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa'i ti ka rigs pa'i rgyan gyi snying po</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་རྣམ་པར་ངེས་པའི་ཏི་ཀ་རིགས་པའི་རྒྱན་གྱི་སྙིང་པོ</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1299-12-31">after 1210 before 1299</date><author ref="person:5510">dar ma dkon mchog</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The author refers more than 100 times anonymously to the views of other Tibetan scholars, who are sometimes identified in glosses in instance (ID:5512), notably: rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786), Phya pa (ID:3831), gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), etc.&#13;
